Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 35/90] java mods: far canopies take the mods' biomes' own tree
 leaves

Far terrain plants Horizon's trees (vanilla's oak, birch, spruce); in the mods' biomes the real ones are the mods' (Biomes O' Plenty's firs and maples). HorizonWorldgen.lodFoliage gives each of the mods' biomes the leaves most of its trees have: vanilla tree features' foliage providers, and a mod's own tree types' leaves read from their encoded form. Far columns in those biomes take them. Vanilla's biomes keep Horizon's trees.

UMP far_truth, 100 mods: coniferous forest far tops are fir leaves like the world's (oak/birch/poplar before).
